!!<*yamlover: $defs: chapter>
A Tour of marklower Links
- |
  A link's target is a **sigiled pointer**. This guide tours every tier: document-relative
  links at [*:1](*:1), project-rooted ones at [*:2](*:2), the parent and current scopes
  at [*:3](*:3), the read-forever aliases and legacy spellings at [*:4](*:4), and external
  targets at [*:5](*:5) — each its own subchapter below.
- Document-relative links
  - |
    A `*:path` link counts from **this document** — the whole guide — however deep you are
    reading, and a bare integer segment is a position. The title is the self-value and
    consumes no index, so the intro is [*:0](*:0) and this section is [*:1](*:1).
  - Going deeper
    - |
      Two levels down, a `*:…` link still counts from the document root: the intro at
      [*:0](*:0), the external-targets section at [*:5](*:5), or this very line
      at [*:1:1:0](*:1:1:0).
- Project-root links
  - |
    A `*::path` link is anchored at the **project root** — the directory yamlover was
    served. Served from the repo, a sibling example is at
    [*::examples:68-math-chapter](*::examples:68-math-chapter), or one formula in it
    at [*::examples:68-math-chapter:2](*::examples:68-math-chapter:2).
- Parent and current scope
  notes: a keyed member of this section — `*notes` lands here
  - |
    A `*name` link resolves in the mapping the prose belongs to — this section's own note
    is at [*notes](*notes). A `*..:` link starts one level up: from here the parent is the
    guide itself, so its intro is at [*..:0](*..:0) and the previous section
    at [*..:2](*..:2).
- Aliases and legacy spellings
  - |
    The **bare colon** form is the same pointer without its sigil, and reads **forever** as
    an alias — the intro at [:0](:0) still lands, though the sigiled spelling is what the
    engine writes when a move rewrites a link.
  - |
    The **slash** spellings are legacy-frozen: the document-relative [/0](/0) and the
    project-rooted [//examples/68-math-chapter](//examples/68-math-chapter) still navigate,
    written never.
- External targets and the reserved sigil
  - |
    Any target with a scheme is an **external** link, opened in a new tab: the KaTeX
    project at [https://katex.org](https://katex.org), or mail the maintainer
    at [mailto:dimskraft@gmail.com](mailto:dimskraft@gmail.com).
  - |
    A `&…` target is **reserved** for bookmarks — it parses but does not yet navigate, so
    its label renders as plain text: [a future bookmark](&some-mark).
